* diff-receiver-sensitivity -- sky130 differential receiver sensitivity at three common-mode points
*
* Circuit body for `klt sim`. The design netlist (design/netlist/differential_receiver.spice)
* is appended by the runner (tb.json "include") and frozen into the immutable snapshot.
* The request supplies the .lib corner section, .temp and the supply sweep (vsup).
*
* One receiver instance per common-mode point (0.8 / 1.65 / 2.5 V), all driven by the
* same differential sweep, so each of the 45 PVT corners yields all three common-mode
* points. Definition:   DP = VCM + VDIFF/2      DM = VCM - VDIFF/2     VDIFF = DP - DM
* VDIFF is swept -400 mV ... +400 mV in 1 mV steps (both polarities, 801 points).
* Common-mode sources are ideal (zero source impedance); the supply is the swept I/O rail.

vsup vdd 0 dc 3.3
vd vd 0 dc 0
ehalf half 0 vol='v(vdd)/2'

* ---- common mode 0.8 V ----
vi08 vdd vdd08 dc 0
vcm08 cm08 0 dc 0.8
edp08 dp08 0 vol='v(cm08)+v(vd)/2'
edm08 dm08 0 vol='v(cm08)-v(vd)/2'
x08 vdd08 0 dp08 dm08 rxd08 differential_receiver

* ---- common mode 1.65 V ----
vi165 vdd vdd165 dc 0
vcm165 cm165 0 dc 1.65
edp165 dp165 0 vol='v(cm165)+v(vd)/2'
edm165 dm165 0 vol='v(cm165)-v(vd)/2'
x165 vdd165 0 dp165 dm165 rxd165 differential_receiver

* ---- common mode 2.5 V ----
vi25 vdd vdd25 dc 0
vcm25 cm25 0 dc 2.5
edp25 dp25 0 vol='v(cm25)+v(vd)/2'
edm25 dm25 0 vol='v(cm25)-v(vd)/2'
x25 vdd25 0 dp25 dm25 rxd25 differential_receiver
